WEBVTT

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:09.000
<v Sophie Lim>Thanks for making time, Michelle. You mentioned you want to buy a condo next year.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:17.000
<v Michelle Ng>Yes, around the middle of next year. But I would rather not sell my investments, the portfolio has done well.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:28.000
<v Sophie Lim>Then one option is a Lombard loan. You borrow against your portfolio and keep your investments. How much you can borrow depends on what the portfolio is worth.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:38.000
<v Sophie Lim>If its value falls below the agreed limit, the bank can ask for more collateral or a repayment, so only borrow what you could repay.

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:46.000
<v Michelle Ng>Understood. I also have the SGD 120,000 from selling my flat in Bangkok, which I could use for the deposit and the costs.

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:55.000
<v Sophie Lim>Good to know, I will include that. How much you can borrow is worked out by our lending specialist, not by me.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:07.000
<v Sophie Lim>I will refer you to our lending specialist this week with your goal and timeline. They work out the amount, then credit risk decides, possibly with conditions.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:15.000
<v Sophie Lim>Your periodic review also has to be up to date before credit can approve, so we need the sale agreement for the Bangkok flat.

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:23.000
<v Michelle Ng>I will upload the sale agreement this week and gather my income documents for the specialist.

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:31.000
<v Michelle Ng>The sale agreement is in Thai, with a certified English translation. Is that acceptable?

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:38.000
<v Sophie Lim>I will ask the compliance team to confirm in writing and come back to you.

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:46.000
<v Sophie Lim>One more thing. Your time deposit ending 4410 matures this week. I will send you the time deposit options by Friday.

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:51.000
<v Michelle Ng>Great, thanks Sophie.
